{"ts": "2026-08-25T01:22:20", "work": "Le Lézard aux plumes d'or", "credit_line": "Louis Broder", "seed_kind": "matrix_agent", "kind": "inert", "index": 61, "counts": {"CONFIRMED": 5, "CORRECTED": 0, "DISPUTED": 0, "UNATTESTED": 0}, "passes": true, "failed": [], "ungrounded": [], "factual_errors": [], "legacy_passes": false, "legacy_failed": ["eventful"], "story": "In 1967, Joan Miró and publisher Louis Broder prepared an edition of lithographs to illustrate Miró's poem *Le Lézard aux plumes d'or*. Shortly after printing, Broder and Miró discovered manufacturing defects in the paper that caused the colors to deteriorate. They rejected the initial printing and ordered the flawed sheets destroyed, but the original printing plates had already been erased. Miró had to create an entirely new series of plates from scratch, delaying the portfolio's official release until 1971.", "pairwise_overlap": [{"a": "Joan Miró", "b": "Louis Broder", "overlap": 0.009}, {"a": "Joan Miró", "b": "Mourlot", "overlap": 0.008}, {"a": "Joan Miró", "b": "Boris Fridman", "overlap": 0.689}, {"a": "Louis Broder", "b": "Mourlot", "overlap": 0.119}, {"a": "Louis Broder", "b": "Boris Fridman", "overlap": 0.011}, {"a": "Mourlot", "b": "Boris Fridman", "overlap": 0.002}], "mean_overlap": 0.14, "max_overlap": 0.689}
